<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Mixed in quiet trade.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Mixed in quiet trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat bids were mixed Wednesday in quiet trade, with weakness tied to an increase in farmer sales, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We saw an increase in farmer selling of both the feed grains and wheat,&quot; said one Montana-based merchandiser. &quot;I guess some guys wanted to take advantage of the MGE rally.&quot;</p>
<p>MGE December wheat futures settled up 4-1/4 cents per bushel at 4.17-1/2, with March up 1/4 at 3.73-1/4, and those modest gains helped to trigger the farmer sales.</p>
<p>U.S. wheat export markets remained sluggish, which also added to the weak tone in cash markets, dealers said.  </p>
